May I ask: In which year was this?<p>&gt;
 I vividly recall coming into the data center for a fortune 50 company, one everyone here would know, and being astonished that they had never heard of Network Attached Storage or RAID
&lt;<p>The thing is: Big companies, even non critical are usually bonded to some frameworks/regulatory standards/etc.<p>So, mentioning that they didnt know NAS or even RAID (which is very old, end of 80s), makes me wondering in which decade this happened?
